---
title: How to Use the Meeting Calendar
description: >-
  See your bookings and your own events on a month, week or day calendar. Add
  an event in any format, including No format, invite people and set reminders.
sidebar:
  order: 11
---
**The Calendar tab shows every meeting booked through your meeting types, plus events you add yourself. Use it to see your day at a glance and to add meetings, calls and blocks of time that did not come from a booking page.**

### **Open the Calendar**

1. Go to **Meetings** in the left menu.
1. Click the **Calendar** tab, next to **Schedules**.

Switch between **Month**, **Week** and **Day**. Use **Previous**, **Next** and **Today** to move around. Times are shown as `12:00 pm` and `01:30 pm`, in your time zone.

Click an item to see its details: format, time, place or link, people, reminders and where it is synced. From there you can **View**, **Edit**, **Reschedule** or **Cancel** it.

### **Filter by Format**

Use **Filter by format** to show only some formats, for example only **Google Meet** meetings.

### **Add an Event**

1. Click **New event**.
1. Enter a **Title**.
1. Pick the **Format**:
   - **No format** – no link, address or phone number. Use it for an internal block, a reminder or anything that is not a call.
   - **In person** – add the **Address**.
   - **Phone** – add the **Phone number**.
   - **Google Meet** – choose the **Google account for the Meet link**. A Meet link is added.
   - **Zoom** – choose the **Zoom account**. A Zoom link is added.
1. Set the **Date**, then the **Start** and **End** time. Turn on **All day** for an event with no time.
1. Check the **Time zone**.
1. Optional: add **Attendees**, a **Description**, **Reminders** and calendar sync (below).
1. Click **Create event**.

An event must start and end on the same day in your workspace time zone.

{% table %}
---
- **Tip:** Google Meet and Zoom need an account connected under **Settings → Meeting Settings → Integrations**. If none is connected, the dialog offers **Connect**.
{% /table %}

### **Invite People**

- Add up to **50 attendees** by email address.
- Turn on **Email an invite** to email each attendee a calendar invite with **Accept** and **Decline** links and an `.ics` file.
- When someone answers, the event shows them as **accepted** or **declined**.
- With **Email an invite** on, changing the time, place or people later sends the attendees an updated invite.

### **Set Reminders**

Add up to **5 reminders**, for example 10 minutes, 1 hour or 1 day before the start.

### **Add the Event to Your Own Calendar**

In the dialog you can also turn on:

- **Add to Google Calendar** – pick the Google account.
- **Add to CalDAV calendar** – pick a connected CalDAV calendar. See [How to Connect a CalDAV Calendar](/meeting-scheduler/how-to-connect-a-caldav-calendar/).

Taskip shows whether each one was saved. If one fails, the event is still saved in Taskip and you can try again by editing it.

### **Book a Slot of a Meeting Type**

Turn on **Link to a meeting type** to book a slot of one of your meeting types instead of a standalone event.

### **Change or Cancel an Event**

- **Edit** – open the event and change anything.
- **Reschedule by dragging** – in the week and day views, drag a timed event to a new time or day.
- **Cancel** – click **Cancel**, add an optional **Reason**, and choose **Email attendees a cancellation** if you want them told. Click **Cancel event**, or **Keep event** to go back.

Events that come from another calendar are read-only. See [How to Connect a CalDAV Calendar](/meeting-scheduler/how-to-connect-a-caldav-calendar/).
